window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-hirata-yousuke"]=[{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p32-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"classroom day 1  initiating class introductions class 1 d classroom after chabashira abruptly leaves  students are in stunned disarray celebrating their 100 000 point deposits without knowing what to do next   everyone  can you please listen to me for a moment   my name s hirata yousuke  back in junior high  lots of people called me yousuke  feel free to use my first name  i guess my hobby is sports in general  but i especially like soccer  i m planning on playing soccer here  too  nice to meet you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: initiating class introductions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.32–34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after Chabashira abruptly leaves. Students are in stunned disarray celebrating their 100,000-point deposits without knowing what to do next.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone, can you please listen to me for a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My name’s Hirata Yousuke. Back in junior high, lots of people called me Yousuke. Feel free to use my first name! I guess my hobby is sports in general, but I especially like soccer. I’m planning on playing soccer here, too. Nice…”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands up with calm confidence, smiling warmly to draw the room&#x27;s attention.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My name’s Hirata Yousuke. Back in junior high, lots of people called me Yousuke. Feel free to use my first name! I guess my hobby is sports in general, but I especially like soccer. I’m planning on playing soccer here, too. Nice to meet you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Effortlessly breaks the ice; commands widespread admiration; girls in class immediately swoon. Proposes orderly self-introductions starting from the front row so classmates can learn each other&#x27;s names before ceremony.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Natural leader, charismatic, genuinely kind, self-effacing, proactive; instinctively steps forward to build group cohesion.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Warm, gentle, inviting, devoid of ego or condescension.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1\">→ After: Mediating Sudō&#x27;s rebellion &amp; Kōenji&#x27;s narcissism<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"mediating sudo s rebellion   koenji s narcissism class 1 d classroom during self introductions   i can t force you to introduce yourself  of course  however  i don t think that getting along with your classmates is a bad thing  if i ve made you uncomfortable  i apologize   they re not a bad bunch  it s my fault  i was being selfish and made people do this   excuse me  can you introduce yourself   um  kouenji kun  what exactly do you mean when you say   anyone who makes me uncomfortable   ah  thank you  i will be careful then   handles koenji s bizarre threat with polite  defusing compliance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mediating Sudō&#x27;s rebellion &amp; Kōenji&#x27;s narcissism<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.37–40<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom during self-introductions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can’t force you to introduce yourself, of course. However, I don’t think that getting along with your classmates is a bad thing. If I’ve made you uncomfortable, I apologize.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“They’re not a bad bunch. It’s my fault. I was being selfish and made people do this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Excuse me, can you introduce yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Encourages Sudō to speak; met with intense delinquent hostility (&quot;Leave me out of it&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Bows deeply to Sudō. When class girls snap at Sudō to defend Hirata, Hirata immediately takes the blame onto himself to protect class unity.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Looks visibly saddened and lonely as Horikita, Sudō, and others walk out of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Politely asks Kōenji to introduce himself; bewildered when Kōenji puts his feet on his desk and threatens to punish &quot;ugly things&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, Kouenji-kun. What exactly do you mean when you say, ‘anyone who makes me uncomfortable’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, thank you. I will be careful then.” (handles Kōenji&#x27;s bizarre threat with polite, defusing compliance).<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gently supports Ayanokōji after he stumbles and freezes during his own botched introduction.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Peacemaker to a fault; absorbs blame to de-escalate tension; refuses to cast out delinquents or oddballs; desperate to keep everyone together.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Patient and forgiving despite Sudō&#x27;s hostility.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Courteous handling of an uncontrollable eccentric.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Encouraging classmate, attempts to welcome him.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p32-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: initiating class introductions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1\">→ After: The cafeteria invitation &amp; female popularity<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"the cafeteria invitation   female popularity class 1 d classroom at lunch bell  day 2   well  i was thinking of heading to the cafeteria  anyone want to come with me   does anyone else want to come","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The cafeteria invitation &amp; female popularity<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.55–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom at lunch bell, Day 2.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I was thinking of heading to the cafeteria. Anyone want to come with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Does anyone else want to come?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands up to invite any lonely or unacquainted classmates to head to the cafeteria together.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Swarmed immediately by eager female classmates who prevent other quiet boys from speaking up. Hirata spots Ayanokōji lingering alone with his hand partially raised and begins to call out his name, but a fashionista girl (Karuizawa Kei) latches onto his arm and whisks him away to lunch, leaving Ayanokōji behind.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Actively looks out for isolated students, but his immense popularity with the girls accidentally hinders him from rescuing quiet male classmates.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Early dynamic: she latches onto his arm as the class&#x27;s top status boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p37-1\">← Before: Mediating Sudō&#x27;s rebellion &amp; Kōenji&#x27;s narcissism<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1\">→ After: Athletic swimming demonstration &amp; universal kindness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"athletic swimming demonstration   universal kindness indoor swimming pool   you think so  thank you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Athletic swimming demonstration &amp; universal kindness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.85–87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Indoor swimming pool.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You think so? Thank you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Swims against Sudō in the second boys&#x27; heat; displays clean, graceful athletic technique, finishing just behind Sudō&#x27;s raw power in approximately 26 seconds.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Swarmed with compliments by class girls (*&quot;You&#x27;re not just good at soccer, you&#x27;re really good at swimming!&quot;*).<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stares in amazement when Kōenji records a blazing 23.22 seconds in the subsequent heat.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Well-rounded athletic ability beyond his primary sport (soccer); humble and courteous recipient of female praise.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p55-1\">← Before: The cafeteria invitation &amp; female popularity<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1\">→ After: Anti-bullying vigil &amp; Horikita&#x27;s isolation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"anti bullying vigil   horikita s isolation classroom 1 d after class   it s about horikita san  actually  i was wondering if something was wrong  some of the girls were talking about it earlier  horikita always seems to be alone   could you possibly tell her to try to get along with people a little   you re right  of course  however  many people have voiced their concerns about it  i absolutely do not want any bullying in our class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Anti-bullying vigil &amp; Horikita&#x27;s isolation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.90<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D after class.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s about Horikita-san, actually. I was wondering if something was wrong. Some of the girls were talking about it earlier. Horikita always seems to be alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Could you possibly tell her to try to get along with people a little?”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re right, of course. However, many people have voiced their concerns about it. I absolutely do not want any bullying in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Intercepts Ayanokōji in the classroom with pure, earnest concern.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Extreme sensitivity to social friction; hyper-vigilant against potential ostracization or bullying before it even begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Concerned for her safety and integration despite her prickly demeanor.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p85-1\">← Before: Athletic swimming demonstration &amp; universal kindness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1\">→ After: Dating Karuizawa &amp; moral unease over point lavishness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"dating karuizawa   moral unease over point lavishness classroom 1 d  then boutique and cafe in keyaki mall   don t you think it s abnormal for a high school student to get 300 000 points as a monthly allowance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Dating Karuizawa &amp; moral unease over point lavishness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.103, 117–118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; then boutique and café in Keyaki Mall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t you think it’s abnormal for a high school student to get 300,000 points as a monthly allowance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Revealed to be dating Class 1-D&#x27;s fashionista girl, Karuizawa Kei, cementing their standing as the premier couple of the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accompanies Karuizawa on a shopping spree in Keyaki Mall, patiently carrying her shopping bags filled with ~30,000 points of designer clothes.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Expresses genuine moral and practical concern over the school&#x27;s financial indulgence; worries that receiving ¥100,000 monthly will ruin the students&#x27; sense of financial discipline and cripple their ability to survive in normal society after graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grounded, socially conscientious; deeply resistant to superficial materialism; looks ahead to real-world consequences after high school.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Gentle, accommodating boyfriend; caters to her luxury shopping while maintaining his own level-headed values.<span class=\"pg\">p.103, 117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p90-1\">← Before: Anti-bullying vigil &amp; Horikita&#x27;s isolation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1\">→ After: Standing up for the class &amp; the podium appeal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"standing up for the class   the podium appeal classroom 1 d  may 1st morning homeroom and subsequent class chaos   sensei  may i please ask you a question  i m afraid i still don t understand  can you please tell us why we didn t receive any points  we won t completely understand otherwise   chiyabashira sensei  i do not recall hearing you explain that to us before  of course  there was never any talk about reducing our points  had that been explained beforehand  i m sure we would have avoided being late or talking during class   well then  could you at least explain in detail how points are added or deducted  we can keep that in mind for future reference   i understand that you re all confused right now  but everyone needs to calm down  even if i was  isn t it better for us to band together so we can turn things around  i understand  however  sitting here whining won t help us right now   it s all right  i should have chosen my words a little more carefully   attention  everyone  before class begins  i want you to listen seriously for a moment  especially you  sudou kun  we didn t get any points this month  this is a serious problem  and one that will have an enormous impact on our daily lives moving forward  it s impossible for us to make it to graduation with zero points  right   of course  therefore  we must earn points next month  to do that  we all need to cooperate with each other  so  please  take care not to be late to class or to talk during the lecture  also  the u","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Standing up for the class &amp; the podium appeal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.121–125, 131–137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st morning homeroom and subsequent class chaos.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sensei, may I please ask you a question? I’m afraid I still don’t understand… Can you please tell us why we didn’t receive any points? We won’t completely understand otherwise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Chiyabashira-sensei. I do not recall hearing you explain that to us before… Of course. There was never any talk about reducing our points. Had that been explained beforehand, I’m sure we would have avoided being late or talking…”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well then, could you at least explain in detail how points are added or deducted? We can keep that in mind for future reference.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the initiative on behalf of the bewildered class to question Chabashira regarding the missing points.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Politely challenges Chabashira’s omission of point deduction rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Chiyabashira-sensei. I do not recall hearing you explain that to us before… Of course. There was never any talk about reducing our points. Had that been explained beforehand, I’m sure we would have avoided being late or talking during class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Expression darkens as Chabashira reveals that merely eliminating infractions will still leave them at zero points next month.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the classroom descends into panic during the break, Hirata steps in to soothe tempers. Yukimura grabs his collar in a rage; Hirata remains completely non-violent.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that you’re all confused right now, but everyone needs to calm down… Even if I was, isn’t it better for us to band together so we can turn things around?… I understand. However, sitting here whining won’t help us right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Kushida defuses Yukimura, Hirata takes accountability gracefully.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s all right. I should have chosen my words a little more carefully.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the teacher’s podium before next period to deliver an impassioned call for class unity.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Attention, everyone. Before class begins, I want you to listen seriously for a moment. Especially you, Sudou-kun… We didn’t get any points this month. This is a serious problem, and one that will have an enormous impact on our daily lives moving forward. It’s impossible for us to make it to graduation with zero points, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Therefore, we must earn points next month. To do that, we all need to cooperate with each other. So, please, take care not to be late to class or to talk during the lecture. Also, the use of cell phones during class is prohibited, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As long as we continue talking during class and being late, our points won’t increase for sure. Although we can’t go below zero points, disruption will, without a doubt, count as strikes against us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudō aggressively rejects his appeal, Hirata bows his head with courteous humility rather than getting angry.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think that there’s anything particularly wrong with what you said, Sudou-kun. I apologize if I made you feel uncomfortable.” (bows his head politely toward the disgruntled Sudou)<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, Sudou-kun, it’s a fact that unless we all cooperate, we won’t get any more points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps down from the podium and stops directly in front of Horikita and Ayanokōji’s desks to personally recruit them into a collective study and improvement effort.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, Ayanokouji-kun, do you have a moment? I want to speak with you about how we can increase our points. I’d like you to join me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is the first trial we’re facing together as a united Class D. So then—”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Horikita rejects him outright (“I refuse. I won’t participate.”), Hirata accepts her rebuff with a self-deprecating wry smile rather than anger.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I…I see. I’m sorry. If you change your mind, I’d love for you to join us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about you, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m sorry for bothering you. If you change your mind, please let me know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quintessential servant-leader; absorbs class hostility without retaliation; persistent dedication to total class unity even when facing toxic rebuffs.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Patiently mediates Sudō&#x27;s outbursts without malice.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Tries earnestly to draw her into the fold; bears her scorn with diplomatic grace.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Values his quiet presence; extends an open-door invitation without coercion.<span class=\"pg\">p.135, 137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p103-1\">← Before: Dating Karuizawa &amp; moral unease over point lavishness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1\">→ After: The midterm study group announcement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"the midterm study group announcement classroom 1 d  lunchtime   chiyabashira sensei mentioned that the midterm is coming up soon  remember that if you fail  you ll be expelled  therefore  i think it would be a good idea to form a study group   if you neglect your studies  you ll get a failing grade and be expelled on the spot  i want to avoid that  however  studying won t just prevent expulsion  it may also help earn points  if we receive high marks  our class s assessment should improve as a result  i asked some of the students who scored high on the test to help prepare a study plan  so  i would like people who are anxious to come join our group  everyone is welcome  of course   starting today at five o clock  we will plan to study in this classroom for two hours a day until the test  if you d like to join us  please come whenever you like  of course  i don t mind if you need to leave partway  that s all i have to say","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The midterm study group announcement<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.152–156<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, lunchtime.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Chiyabashira-sensei mentioned that the midterm is coming up soon. Remember that if you fail, you’ll be expelled. Therefore, I think it would be a good idea to form a study group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you neglect your studies, you’ll get a failing grade and be expelled on the spot. I want to avoid that. However, studying won’t just prevent expulsion; it may also help earn points. If we receive high marks, our class’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Starting today at five o’clock, we will plan to study in this classroom for two hours a day until the test. If you’d like to join us, please come whenever you like. Of course, I don’t mind if you need to leave partway. That’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the floor when everyone rises for lunch and announces his own study group project, staring directly at Sudou during his grand speech.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you neglect your studies, you’ll get a failing grade and be expelled on the spot. I want to avoid that. However, studying won’t just prevent expulsion; it may also help earn points. If we receive high marks, our class’s assessment should improve as a result. I asked some of the students who scored high on the test to help prepare a study plan. So, I would like people who are anxious to come join our group. Everyone is welcome, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Starting today at five o’clock, we will plan to study in this classroom for two hours a day until the test. If you’d like to join us, please come whenever you like. Of course, I don’t mind if you need to leave partway. That’s all I have to say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Several failing students immediately get up and join; Sudou, Ike, and Yamauchi notably stay seated — the three he most wanted (especially Sudou).<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Proactive crisis leadership paired with personal charisma; his group becomes the default destination for the class&#x27;s struggling students.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Relationship rocky since Sudou stomped all over his introduction game; targets Sudou with a direct stare during the speech, but Sudou averts his gaze in a Tch.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p121-1\">← Before: Standing up for the class &amp; the podium appeal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1\">→ After: The avoided rival &amp; the beneficiary of the test-change notice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"the avoided rival   the beneficiary of the test change notice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The avoided rival &amp; the beneficiary of the test-change notice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.213, 226<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Unseen presence shaping logistics: his own study group meets during lunch, which is the main reason Horikita&#x27;s group relocates to the library — she absolutely does not want contact with his group.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Designated by Ayanokōji (via Kushida) as a recipient of Chabashira&#x27;s revised test-material list, ensuring his larger group also studies the right topics.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p152-1\">← Before: The midterm study group announcement<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1\">→ After: Exam-morning confidence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"chabashira-sae hirata-yousuke","q":"exam morning confidence   we ve studied diligently these past few weeks  i don t think that anyone will fail","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Exam-morning confidence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’ve studied diligently these past few weeks. I don’t think that anyone will fail.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Answers Chabashira&#x27;s exam-day roll call with public confidence in the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Drawn out by her: “Oh my. You sound quite confident, Hirata.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p213-1\">← Before: The avoided rival &amp; the beneficiary of the test-change notice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: The first to protest the red line<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"the first to protest the red line   s sensei  is sudou kun really being expelled  is there no way to save him   could we possibly see sudou kun s answer sheet   there are no mistakes   his darkening expression after the full audit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The first to protest the red line<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246–248<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“S-sensei. Is Sudou-kun really being expelled? Is there no way to save him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Could we possibly see Sudou-kun’s answer sheet?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There…are no mistakes.” (his darkening expression after the full audit)<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Presses Chabashira for the results announcement and is calmly brushed off (&quot;You should have passed quite easily&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> First to challenge Sudou&#x27;s expulsion — even though Sudou hates him — demanding the answer sheet be audited; verifies every problem himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Moral consistency under hostility: fights for the classmate who insulted him while others silently feel relieved.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v1-p240-1\">← Before: Exam-morning confidence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 1  decoding horikita in public  the class leader  hirata yousuke  answered for her    after horikita bait and silences the class on  get something   i believe that horikita san is referring to the deductions we incurred throughout april and may  in other words  we didn t see a reduction in points for talking in class or being late","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: decoding Horikita in public<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.17–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;The class leader, Hirata Yousuke, answered for her.&quot; — after Horikita bait-and-silences the class on &quot;get something.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I believe that Horikita-san is referring to the deductions we incurred throughout April and May. In other words, we didn’t see a reduction in points for talking in class or being late.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads peers&#x27; half-thoughts accurately and translates them for the room without seeking credit; AK: &quot;The sharp-witted Hirata hadn’t missed a beat. Splendid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Named by AK as an expert-advice pillar (&quot;If it were Horikita or Hirata here, they’d probably be able to give expert advice.&quot;) — but unusable on Sudou&#x27;s case because &quot;Sudou hates Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Still the object of Sudou&#x27;s hatred from the fake-expulsion episode; Hirata is not in the crisis&#x27;s inner circle at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK holds him up as the standard he himself declines to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  the one standing voice for sudou stands in support of kushida s appeal for sudou   hirata  the class hero  uttered those words as he stood in support of kushida  his appearance was dashing  and he clearly wasn t drunk on the same anti sudou kool aid as everyone else  after school he organizes the canvassing as a team  ak names  the hero   gal team  that he leads with karuizawa  searching campus themselves   umm  so why hasn t this issue been resolved already    ak calls it  a rather reasonable question  the first thing anyone asks chabashira after the announcement   i want to believe him   if a student in another class were casting doubt on him  i could understand it   but i think it s wrong to doubt a fellow classmate right away  shouldn t friends do everything within their power to help someone in need","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands in support of Kushida&#x27;s appeal for Sudou: &quot;Hirata, the class hero, uttered those words as he stood in support of Kushida. His appearance was dashing, and he clearly wasn’t drunk on the same anti-Sudou Kool-Aid as everyone else.&quot; After school he organizes the canvassing as a team: AK names &quot;the Hero &amp; Gal Team&quot; that he leads with Karuizawa, searching campus themselves.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Umm. So why hasn’t this issue been resolved already?” — AK calls it &quot;a rather reasonable question&quot;, the first thing anyone asks Chabashira after the announcement.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to believe him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If a student in another class were casting doubt on him, I could understand it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I think it’s wrong to doubt a fellow classmate right away. Shouldn’t friends do everything within their power to help someone in need?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His stance converts the room by example, not argument — AK: &quot;Starting with those three, we launched our investigation to prove Sudou’s innocence&quot;, and &quot;Hirata, Kushida, and Karuizawa had attracted the rest of our class’s admiration.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The conversion is fragile and AK says so plainly: &quot;Though they probably mocked him in their hearts, they would help Sudou a little bit&quot; — the class follows the lead, it does not change its opinion.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Publicly defends the classmate who refuses him privately; the Year 1, Vol. 2 ch2 note stands — Sudou will not ask him, so the defence costs Hirata nothing with Sudou and gains Sudou nothing with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: decoding Horikita in public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 0  the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has his team s canvass produced records  not results   i heard that hirata and his group hadn t obtained any valuable information  they d recorded the names of the people to whom they d spoken  and occasionally taken notes on their cell phones  the cost of that line on himself  watched by the class s worst judge   ike  who considered hirata a goody two shoes  eyed him suspiciously   even if sudou was at fault    however  hirata nodded without a moment s hesitation  it was as though he believed self sacrifice was unimportant  ike immediately looked downward  as if pressed under the weight of hirata s noble intentions   then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again    and the reason he gives   it s only been three months since we started here    ak   our classroom hero didn t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech  the girls immediately blushed in response   i understand how you feel  however  it can be dangerous to cling to our points and lose sight of reality  the most important thing is to treasure our friends as much as possible   you know  if you think back on it now  it was obvious from the start    the one student who had already connected the school s signals   remember what our p e  instructor higashiyama sensei said when we went to the pool  he said the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points  that was a stepping stone to prepare us for oth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–72<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His team&#x27;s canvass produced records, not results: &quot;I heard that Hirata and his group hadn’t obtained any valuable information. They’d recorded the names of the people to whom they’d spoken, and occasionally taken notes on their cell phones.&quot; The cost of that line on himself, watched by the class&#x27;s worst judge: &quot;Ike, who considered Hirata a goody two shoes, eyed him suspiciously. &#x27;Even if Sudou was at fault?&#x27; ... However, Hirata nodded without a moment’s hesitation. It was as though he believed self-sacrifice was unimportant. Ike immediately looked downward, as if pressed under the weight of Hirata’s noble intentions.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again,&quot; — and the reason he gives: &quot;It’s only been three months since we started here.&quot; — AK: &quot;Our classroom hero didn’t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech.…<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand how you feel. However, it can be dangerous to cling to our points and lose sight of reality. The most important thing is to treasure our friends as much as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You know, if you think back on it now, it was obvious from the start.&quot; — the one student who had already connected the school&#x27;s signals: &quot;Remember what our P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei said when we went to the pool? He…<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again,&quot; — and the reason he gives: &quot;It’s only been three months since we started here.&quot; — AK: &quot;Our classroom hero didn’t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech. The girls immediately blushed in response.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You know, if you think back on it now, it was obvious from the start.&quot; — the one student who had already connected the school&#x27;s signals: &quot;Remember what our P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei said when we went to the pool? He said the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points. That was a stepping stone to prepare us for other opportunities. It seems plausible, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His memory of a teacher&#x27;s throwaway promise is the evidence that the club-points track exists, and Ike cannot supply any of it: &quot;Ike scratched his head and slumped. &#x27;I don’t remember,&#x27; he said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 2 4 3  he will greet sakura but not ask her  and he physically stops sudou he invites ak into his own social life  girlfriend included   oh  that reminds me  if you re up for it  we should hang out sometime soon  what do you think  and  are you fine with my girlfriend coming  too    and reads ak s refusal when ak himself cannot   i m sorry  do you not really want to  when sudou kicks a desk apart and walks on koenji  he is the only one who moves   he was the only boy able to move in this awful situation  my heart pounded in my chest   good morning  ayanokouji kun     hirata called to me  his expression as fresh and friendly as usual  the sweet yet subtle fragrance of flowers always emanated from him  why he does not go to the witness himself   me  no  i m going to greet her  that s all  i ve wanted to talk to her since she s always by herself  but as a guy i don t want to come off as forceful or anything  also  if i asked karuizawa san to talk with her  that might cause a few problems   i think that for the time being  we ll just wait for more information from kushida san    the hero s plan is to let someone else do the asking  his reason for briefing ak at all   not for any particular reason  i guess it s because you have a connection to horikita san  she doesn t talk to anyone except for you  so i thought you d pass it along    ak   there was no real reason for him to tell me any of this  i wasn t really part of the team   all right  that s enough  calm down  you tw","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.83–84, p.92–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He invites AK into his own social life, girlfriend included: &quot;Oh, that reminds me. If you’re up for it, we should hang out sometime soon. What do you think?&quot; and &quot;Are you fine with my girlfriend coming, too?&quot; — and reads AK&#x27;s refusal when AK himself cannot: &quot;I’m sorry. Do you not really want to?&quot; When Sudou kicks a desk apart and walks on Kōenji, he is the only one who moves: &quot;He was the only boy able to move in this awful situation. My heart pounded in my chest.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — &quot;Hirata called to me, his expression as fresh and friendly as usual. The sweet yet subtle fragrance of flowers always emanated from him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Why he does not go to the witness himself: &quot;Me? No. I’m going to greet her, that’s all. I’ve wanted to talk to her since she’s always by herself, but as a guy I don’t want to come off as forceful or anything. Also, if I asked…<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think that for the time being, we’ll just wait for more information from Kushida-san.&quot; — the hero&#x27;s plan is to let someone else do the asking.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Why he does not go to the witness himself: &quot;Me? No. I’m going to greet her, that’s all. I’ve wanted to talk to her since she’s always by herself, but as a guy I don’t want to come off as forceful or anything. Also, if I asked Karuizawa-san to talk with her, that might cause a few problems.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His reason for briefing AK at all: &quot;Not for any particular reason. I guess it’s because you have a connection to Horikita-san. She doesn’t talk to anyone except for you, so I thought you’d pass it along.&quot; — AK: &quot;There was no real reason for him to tell me any of this. I wasn’t really part of the team.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;All right, that’s enough. Calm down, you two,&quot; — and he puts the blame on both sides in front of the class: &quot;Sudou-kun. You certainly are part of the problem here. But Kouenji-kun, you’re in the wrong, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Stop it already. I don’t want to see my friends fight…&quot; is Kushida&#x27;s; his is the follow-up that picks a side for the record: &quot;It’s just like Kushida says. I don’t know about Kouenji-kun, but I’m your ally, Sudou-kun.&quot; — AK: &quot;Hirata was way too cool. It would’ve been fitting if he changed his name to &#x27;Hero.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His last line to Sudou is the school&#x27;s argument, not his own feeling: &quot;I’m going to stop this. Sudou-kun, you should act more mature. If you cause another huge disturbance, the school’s evaluation of you will only worsen. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Then, alone with Kōenji after Sudou slams out: &quot;Kouenji-kun. I don’t intend to compel you to help. But you were wrong to blame him.&quot; — and AK&#x27;s conclusion from watching the pair: &quot;Watching their bizarre interaction unfold, I realized that our class lacked unity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He never asks the witness anything, never challenges Horikita&#x27;s write-off of Sudou, and stops a fight by citing the school&#x27;s evaluation — leadership that avoids being the one who pressures anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.7, §4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 7   4 11  he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.7, §4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.120, p.149<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Kushida, on the phone about the corridor fight: &quot;I couldn’t even move. Hirata-kun was so amazing, though.&quot; — Ayanokōji&#x27;s jealous gloss on the praise: &quot;Hearing her praise Hirata like that made me a little jealous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The couple the class copies: &quot;It seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like Hirata and Karuizawa.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is invoked as a teacher of social technique by the one person who watches him most closely: &quot;What should I do? Please, Hirata. Teach me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She credits him and herself, in the same breath, for Class D&#x27;s cohesion: &quot;Class D was able to come together, thanks to you and Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> In the second half of Chapter 4 he appears only as other students&#x27; measure of themselves; his own scenes ended at p.93.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7: a passing mention in the verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 7  a passing mention in the verdict","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: a passing mention in the verdict<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is named once, in Horikita’s summary of pending rewards for the hearing — Kushida’s and his actions &quot;would be rewarded as well&quot; — and appears nowhere else in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.7, §4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0 2 2  the leader tries to hold a class that won t hold still deck of the liner  he pulls ayanokoji into the group the moment he appears","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.16, p.30–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; he pulls Ayanokōji into the group the moment he appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Called over as rescue; Hirata himself is too busy — &quot;Miyake-kun looks like he&#x27;s having trouble&quot; — and leaves for the cabins.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Asked why he isn&#x27;t with her: “We just kind of take things at our own pace.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads the watch rule as safety kit, not control: &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Opened the rules huddle that Ike&#x27;s complaints fracture into factions.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Breaks his own neutrality on the toilet: &quot;I&#x27;ve thought it over, and I believe we should install one toilet first&quot; — then beats Yukimura&#x27;s objection with the arithmetic of thirty-plus students sharing one box.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s verdict on the method: &quot;It wasn’t just to provoke arguments; he was convinced that he’d get their approval eventually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 8  the river  the 120 point speech  and taking ibuki in receives ike s river report and moves the class toward a base camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Receives Ike&#x27;s river report and moves the class toward a base camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Praised the find — &quot;Amazing, Ike-kun!&quot; — then takes his name to Chabashira as leader-candidate filing errand-boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Files Horikita&#x27;s name and hands her the card; orchestrates the fake collective touch to hide the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Breaks up the Ike–Shinohara round two and buys time: &quot;Let’s try breaking apart for a bit. We still have some time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Asks Ayanokōji for branches, apologetically — &quot;I can’t force you to agree&quot; — because light is necessary whether or not points get spent.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s centrepiece speech: sets the realistic floor at 120 points left, walks the class through the meal maths (10-point sets, 12 meals, 120 points), then reframes endurance as upside — &quot;If we can find drinking water for the week, we’ll save fifty points or more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji&#x27;s read: &quot;Anyone else could have come up with this, but Hirata’s tone and presentation sold it. He’d performed flawlessly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Takes the injured Class C girl in: &quot;We can’t just leave someone in trouble. We all think so.&quot; — and turns the spy question on its head: &quot;If you really were a spy, you wouldn’t want to be chased out, would you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Leaves Sakura out of the Ibuki escort — Ayanokōji reads it as pretty-boy thoughtfulness.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Distributes the evening meal while Kushida feeds Ibuki from her own group&#x27;s portion.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei kanzaki-ryuuji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  the morning watch and the point arithmetic awake before the class in the crowded tent  greets ayanokoji slipping out  his back aching without a mattress   if you include kouenji kun s penalty  we spent almost 100 points yesterday  i told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we d be left with 120 points  but now i m not even sure about that  i guess the anxiety woke me   i m only doing this because i like it  if my hard work makes everyone in class happy  then i m satisfied  but it s surprisingly difficult   i wonder if our strategy s wrong  even if we can t beat the other classes  i thought it d be good for us to unify on this test  that s the real reason i don t want them to discover our leader   thank you  coming from you  that honestly makes me really happy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Awake before the class in the crowded tent; greets Ayanokōji slipping out, his back aching without a mattress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you include Kouenji-kun&#x27;s penalty, we spent almost 100 points yesterday. I told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we&#x27;d be left with 120 points, but now I&#x27;m not even sure about that. I guess the anxiety woke me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I&#x27;m only doing this because I like it. If my hard work makes everyone in class happy, then I&#x27;m satisfied. But it&#x27;s surprisingly difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder if our strategy&#x27;s wrong. Even if we can&#x27;t beat the other classes, I thought it&#x27;d be good for us to unify on this test. That&#x27;s the real reason I don&#x27;t want them to discover our leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Cannot answer the Class A question — “That&#x27;s hard to answer. Aiming for the upper classes means forcing everyone… I&#x27;m sorry, I need to think on it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Adjusts his position so Ayanokōji can read the manual comfortably — “small acts of consideration” noted from the other side.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Carries her heart-bedazzled gifts in his pack and confirms it — “Spot on. How&#x27;d you guess?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Greets Kanzaki by name and accepts the apology for the early visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Coming from you, that honestly makes me really happy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Plans the sleeping-arrangement poll at the river, then after roll call assigns roles to the reliable students — Class D&#x27;s point-saving start.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 4  4 3  the corn report at base camp when ayanokoji cuts out of yamauchi s rant to reach him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At base camp when Ayanokōji cuts out of Yamauchi’s rant to reach him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets the corn report first-hand; soon afterward students are organized into a team that brings the harvest back.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the search and the secret<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 6  the search and the secret called out of the tent by shinohara  he rouses the boys and runs the luggage inspection that ends with the stolen underwear in his own hands   ah  hirata kun  i m sorry  but can you please wake all of the boys  it s serious   i understand  i think if i shout  they ll come   i know that you re not the culprit  hirata kun  but for the time being  let s check the boys  luggage   well  there s no evidence that the boys stole it  maybe karuizawa lost it   i don t want to think there s a criminal among us   for now  we ll try gathering the guys together and talking it out  can you please give us a little time   i don t doubt you guys  but we won t solve the problem like this   it might be better to just accept the baggage inspection with dignity and prove your innocence   of course  i ll open up my luggage first   as miserable as this might be  i think you guys ll have to do it  are you okay with that   we searched everyone s bags  none of us did it   yeah  there s no doubt  none of the boys are the culprit   hey  hirata kun  could they have hidden it in their pockets  ike kun and yamauchi kun  and even ayanokouji kun were whispering a little earlier  it s got me curious   okay  if it convinces the girls  fine  however  if i don t find anything  i want you to stop investigating the boys   i m sorry  it ll be over soon   ayanokouji kun doesn t have them either   those three didn t take them   did you take karuizawa s underwear  ayanokouji kun   i beli","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the search and the secret<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.159–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Called out of the tent by Shinohara, he rouses the boys and runs the luggage inspection that ends with the stolen underwear in his own hands.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Ah, Hirata-kun. I’m sorry, but can you please wake all of the boys? It’s serious,”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand. I think if I shout, they’ll come.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “I know that you’re not the culprit, Hirata-kun. But for the time being, let’s check the boys’ luggage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>37 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there’s no evidence that the boys stole it. Maybe Karuizawa lost it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want to think there’s a criminal among us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For now, we’ll try gathering the guys together and talking it out. Can you please give us a little time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> The one boy exempt from her contempt; his word buys the others time.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t doubt you guys, but we won’t solve the problem like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It might be better to just accept the baggage inspection with dignity and prove your innocence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. I’ll open up my luggage first,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens his own bag first so that no other boy can refuse the inspection.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As miserable as this might be, I think you guys’ll have to do it. Are you okay with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We searched everyone’s bags. None of us did it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. There’s no doubt. None of the boys are the culprit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the two reporting lines untagged after Ike calls Shinohara over; recorded here as the inspector’s report.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata-kun. Could they have hidden it in their pockets? Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun, and even Ayanokouji-kun were whispering a little earlier. It’s got me curious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. If it convinces the girls, fine. However, if I don’t find anything, I want you to stop investigating the boys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. It’ll be over soon,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pats Ayanokōji down, feels the cloth in his back pocket, and reports finding nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Does not doubt him for a moment, yet keeps the finding to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun doesn’t have them either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those three didn’t take them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you…take Karuizawa’s underwear, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you. You’re not that kind of person. But why did you have them in your pocket?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s all right with you, may I hold onto the underwear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the worst-case scenario, if I’m made out to be the culprit, I would take the least amount of damage. I am her boyfriend, more or less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the underwear into a vinyl toilet bag — the Joker in a deck of cards.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. So it definitely wasn’t you. But I don’t think Ike-kun or Yamauchi-kun did it, either. If they were the culprits, they probably wouldn’t put the underwear in their own bags. They would have hidden it in another place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But we did find out one piece of bad news here. If the underwear came out of Ike-kun’s bag, then there’s a high chance that the culprit is someone in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re not the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun. That’s why I saved you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s not all I want to say. I want you to help me find the real culprit, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think people, both guys and girls, will be uneasy until the thief’s found. To be honest, it would probably be best if I found the culprit, but it looks like it’ll be difficult to get everyone together…”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you! Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun!”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you do happen to find the culprit, I want you to tell me first. I definitely do not want you to tell anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that information becomes public knowledge, our class will suffer a huge blow. I want to avoid that. That’s why I want to find a peaceful method of settling things with the culprit. If it’s coming from me, I think that we’ll be able to resolve the issue through talking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hide it? That’s a poor choice of words, but there’s nothing I can do about it if people take it that way. Even if one of the guys turns out to the be the culprit, I think it’s better that the truth be concealed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The printed line reads “turns out to the be the culprit” — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Widens his eyes while making the appeal for secrecy; the narration calls his calm almost too calm, a little eerie.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Well then, I’ll be getting back to work.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration marks one contradiction: right after saying he believes Ayanokōji, he insists the truth be concealed.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p142-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: the corn report<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 6  6 1  the meeting that splits the camp runs the meeting where karuizawa s fear turns into a ban on the boys  and takes the mediator s role once more   could everyone please gather around   we can t trust the guys  it s absolutely impossible for us to stay in the same place as them   but there would be problems if the guys and girls lived apart  don t you think  the test is almost over  because we re all friends  we need to believe in and cooperate with one another   you might be right  but we can t stand being in the same place as underwear thieves   okay  i ll help  it might take some time  though  is that okay   yeah  hirata kun is the only one we can trust   huh  hirata kun is not the culprit  what a stupid thing to say  why don t you go jump off a cliff   karuizawa san  it would be great if we could have another guy here help me out  is that okay   b but how can i trust anyone other than you  hirata kun   i understand what everyone wants to say here  but i disagree with suspecting a classmate without evidence  there shouldn t be anyone in our class who d do such an awful thing   i don t know  but i don t want to doubt my classmates","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Runs the meeting where Karuizawa’s fear turns into a ban on the boys, and takes the mediator’s role once more.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Could everyone please gather around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “We can’t trust the guys. It’s absolutely impossible for us to stay in the same place as them!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But there would be problems if the guys and girls lived apart, don’t you think? The test is almost over. Because we’re all friends, we need to believe in and cooperate with one another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening call of the meeting is left untagged in the translation; the narration has his meeting already begun as Ayanokōji steps out.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves this answer to Karuizawa untagged; she shakes her head at it in the next line.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might be right. But we can’t stand being in the same place as underwear thieves!”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> He cannot force her back when the victim says the boys cannot be trusted.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I’ll help. It might take some time, though. Is that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The only boy she trusts; she blushes when he agrees to help her side.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, Hirata-kun is the only one we can trust.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Hirata-kun is not the culprit. What a stupid thing to say. Why don’t you go jump off a cliff?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san, it would be great if we could have another guy here help me out. Is that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Adopts the role of mediator once again when Karuizawa is on the verge of losing her temper.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “B-but…how can I trust anyone other than you, Hirata-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what everyone wants to say here, but I disagree with suspecting a classmate without evidence. There shouldn’t be anyone in our class who’d do such an awful thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know, but I don’t want to doubt my classmates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the search and the secret<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2–§6.3: the stakes, the points, the fever<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 6  6 2 6 3  the stakes  the points  the fever pitches the girls  second tent at ayanokoji s side after the split  then is pulled away by karuizawa and the other girls   i m sorry  i ve put you in a tough spot again   oh  it s not all bad  i do it freely   work so hard  i don t intend to work all that hard  i just do what needs to be done   i think this special test isn t actually some kind of battle  but more an important opportunity for us all to become closer  that s why i want to cherish this moment  i m glad to work hard for that   ah  i still have work left to do  though   no  but it s hard for one person to   s sorry  thank you  i ll be right back   exactly  trustworthy hirata kun has kept his mouth shut about it   karuizawa san reported this to hirata kun  so he definitely knew about it  but you didn t know  nor did he inform anyone else  i think he absolutely should have shared this information","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2–§6.3: the stakes, the points, the fever<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.180–189<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pitches the girls’ second tent at Ayanokōji’s side after the split, then is pulled away by Karuizawa and the other girls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. I’ve put you in a tough spot again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, it’s not all bad. I do it freely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Work so hard? I don’t intend to work all that hard. I just do what needs to be done.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration opens on him: a really cool guy, principled, taking the initiative on troublesome work and answering opponents respectfully.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think this special test isn’t actually some kind of battle, but more an important opportunity for us all to become closer. That’s why I want to cherish this moment. I’m glad to work hard for that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Works the stakes beside him and gets the straight answer about why he works so hard.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, I still have work left to do, though,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, but it’s hard for one person to¾”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The printed line ends in a broken¾ glyph — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry. Thank you. I’ll be right back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Is pulled off the stakes by the girls and left to Ayanokōji, who finishes the work alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. Trustworthy Hirata-kun has kept his mouth shut about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa-san reported this to Hirata-kun, so he definitely knew about it. But you didn’t know, nor did he inform anyone else. I think he absolutely should have shared this information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kept quiet about the girls’ twelve-point spending, known to him through Karuizawa’s report.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: the last forage<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 6  6 4  the last forage reports a quiet night  then sorts the class into teams for one last search for food   i m glad  we haven t had any incidents   would it be better if we went  too   no  ike kun  sudou kun  i want you two to continue fishing  we don t have enough time to instruct the other students how to do it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: the last forage<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.192–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reports a quiet night, then sorts the class into teams for one last search for food.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m glad. We haven’t had any incidents,”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Would it be better if we went, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No. Ike-kun, Sudou-kun, I want you two to continue fishing. We don’t have enough time to instruct the other students how to do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps Ike and Sudou on the river and sets the search groups by volunteers, with Ayanokōji as backup.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p180-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2–§6.3: the stakes, the points, the fever<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire and the crack<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 6  6 7  the fire and the crack at the fire behind the temporary toilet   the survival manual was in his bag  and he takes the blame before the culprit   i m responsible for this  the manual was in my bag  we piled the bags up in front of the tent and i didn t think that someone would steal anything in the daytime  but first  we need to extinguish this fire properly   why  who could do something like this  why can t we all just get along   thank you   we need to discuss this incident properly   right  most of class d witnessed the fire  i m sure they ll want to know the truth   wait a minute  everyone  please  calm down  let s talk about this   hirata  tell us what to do   why why is this happening  it s just like back then   why was i doing this  why was i doing all this until now   ike s calling for you   rain   it d be good for you to help ike and the others  we have to keep our stuff dry   y yeah  we need to take care of everything quickly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.7: the fire and the crack<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.206–211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the fire behind the temporary toilet — the survival manual was in his bag, and he takes the blame before the culprit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m responsible for this. The manual was in my bag. We piled the bags up in front of the tent and I didn’t think that someone would steal anything in the daytime. But first, we need to extinguish this fire properly…”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why? Who could do something like this? Why can’t we all just get along?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes to the river to douse the fire instead of hunting the culprit, and crushes a plastic bottle in his fist.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The eternal peacemaker cracks — the narration calls the shift in his personality rather terrifying.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need…to discuss this incident properly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. Most of Class D witnessed the fire. I’m sure they’ll want to know the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply carries no speaker tag; it sits under his own call to discuss, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands his water to Ayanokōji and goes into the circle to mediate.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute, everyone. Please, calm down. Let’s talk about this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands dazed in the middle of the confrontation instead of stopping it.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata, tell us what to do!”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why…why is this happening? It’s just like back then…”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page never says what “back then” refers to.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stares off into nothingness through the rising rain and does not notice Ayanokōji approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why was I doing this? Why was I doing all this until now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ike’s calling for you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Rain…”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’d be good for you to help Ike and the others. We have to keep our stuff dry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-yeah. We need to take care of everything quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou watches the shock from the side and names the danger of a breakdown before anyone else.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Since the test began he has carried one burden after another; the underwear theft and the fire have turned him unhinged and stormy as the weather.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p192-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: the last forage<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p240-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the rest area and the deck<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p240-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken ryuuen-kakeru ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 7  the rest area and the deck brings paper cups to the rest area  thanks ayanokoji and sudou for the week  and carries the beach exchange with ryuuen until mashima s megaphone cuts it short   good work  both of you  thank you for everything you did this week  you really saved us   i should be thanking you  you covered for me  the class loner  also  you covered for me being late for roll call  and the fact that horikita retired   i couldn t blame you when i heard the reason  besides  horikita san gave us some really important information   do you believe what she said   she isn t the type to speak irresponsibly  that s why you get along with her  right   i d be lying if i said there wasn t any risk  but i had to help horikitasan   that s a friend   wait  what did you say  what are you talking about   oh  hey there  sycophants  what happened to suzune   i know you ve been chasing suzune s ass  we were together before  you know   throw that away for me   what a stupid thing to say  huh  pick up your own trash  jerk   but picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage   calm down  sudou kun  here  i ll throw it away   who are you  more importantly  where s suzune  i ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom   the next time you say something stupid  i ll kill you  sudou growled   horikita san retired yesterday  she s not here   retired  suzune  she doesn t seem like that kind of girl   that s what we should be saying to you class c people  you used up all of your points  r","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the rest area and the deck<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.240–246<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Brings paper cups to the rest area, thanks Ayanokōji and Sudou for the week, and carries the beach exchange with Ryuuen until Mashima’s megaphone cuts it short.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Good work, both of you. Thank you for everything you did this week. You really saved us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I should be thanking you. You covered for me, the class loner. Also, you covered for me being late for roll call, and the fact that Horikita retired.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I couldn’t blame you when I heard the reason. Besides, Horikita-san gave us some really important information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands him and Sudou the two paper cups he was carrying.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you believe what she said?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She isn’t the type to speak irresponsibly. That’s why you get along with her, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration calls him the one who would protect an ally even if it risked his pure reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d be lying if I said there wasn’t any risk, but I had to help Horikitasan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, what did you say? What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finds Class C emptied with the pair — Ibuki nowhere on the sandy beach — Ryuuen alone, cup in hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, hey there, sycophants. What happened to Suzune?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you’ve been chasing Suzune’s ass. We were together before, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Throw that away for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a stupid thing to say. Huh? Pick up your own trash, jerk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, Sudou-kun. Here, I’ll throw it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hurriedly picks up the cup Sudou trampled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you? More importantly, where’s Suzune? I’ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next time you say something stupid, I’ll kill you,” Sudou growled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jumps in and pulls Sudou away from Ryuuen before fists can fly.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san retired yesterday. She’s not here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Retired? Suzune? She doesn’t seem like that kind of girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His reply is untagged and is recorded as his; “I thought you retired, Ryuuen-kun.” and the interrupted reply “That’s¾” are left out as chapter attribution gaps; the broken three-quarter mark is kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what we should be saying to you Class C people. You used up all of your points, right? Don’t make us laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have 125 points remaining. I think we’ll be quite fine,”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re going to expose a class leader?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hold on a minute. What are you talking about, huh?! I-If you’re telling the truth, then…”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Bwah ha ha ha! Hey, check it out! You guys have zero points after all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll explain everything. Well, Ryuuen-kun, if you’ll excuse us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks toward the boat with Ike and Sudou while Sudou raises a middle finger at Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You jerk, Kouenji! We lost thirty points because of you. You know what I’m talking about, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, Karuizawa-san, I think you should talk to Horikita-san first, don’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is attributed only to “he”; he has just proposed the talk, so it is recorded as him.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.7: the fire and the crack<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
